{"author":"reconciler","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Our goal is to integrate self improvement into rebar's review process so that friction during development, bugs after release, and user observations flow into improvements to the review process without the need for dedicated epics and design by users. Our intent is to provide 3 options for the feature: off (no auto improvement), suggestion (improvements require user approval), and fully autonomous (improvements happen automatically).\nDuring brainstorming, start with the following information gathering. These steps should be completed as part of brainstorming, not as part of the epic implementation.\n1. Look at this project's history of improving the review process, specifically at criteria additions or modifications. \n2. Research skills, prompts, and agentic development systems that involve self-improvement. How do they gather information during the development workflow? How do they decide what guidance to preserve? How do they handle growth of guidance over time to avoid unbounded context usage? What gotchas have they encountered?\n3. Search for research on self-improving agentic systems from 2026, focusing on those with data or code to support their conclusions. How do they solve the problem of unreliable agentic judgment when determining what improvements are worth making? How do they prevent new improvements from causing regression? What other problems are will documented in self-improving systems?\nConsider whether we should implement shadow criteria to evaluate self improvement before they are visible to users. Shadow criteria would be evaluated in pass 1 and 2 of the review process as normal, with the results recorded in a tracking file, but would always be dropped by pass 3. This could allow us to gather data to support the value of a new criteria before promoting it to normal use. We would want to limit the number of shadow criteria at a time to avoid excessive token use and wall clock costs."}},"env_id":"reconciler","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785047256772705031,"uuid":"9feeb99d-f386-44fe-bb39-31839db5045e"}